:: StoryTitle
Lamp Room


:: StoryData
{
  "ifid": "3F1E7A20-4C55-4B4E-9F2E-0C1D6B8A5E31",
  "format": "Harlowe",
  "format-version": "3.3.9",
  "start": "Landing"
}


:: Landing
(set: $lamp to false)
(set: $coins to 2)
The stair ends at a door nobody has painted this century.
[[Try the handle|Handle]]


:: Handle
(set: $lamp to true)
The handle turns, which is more than you expected.
(if: $coins >= 2)[
You still have the fare in your pocket, for whatever that is worth now.
](else:)[
Your pockets are empty and the night is not over.
]
(text-style:"underline")[The room beyond is dark.]
[[Go in|Inside]]
[[Turn back|Landing]]


:: Inside
(track: 'doorClose', 'play')
Somebody has left a lamp burning on the sill.
(if: $lamp)[The handle is still warm in your hand.]
(if: $name is "")[
Nobody has asked your name yet.
[[Say nothing|Inside]]
]
(print: $coins) coins, and nothing to spend them on.
The window looks out on the ford, which is still going.
